  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "When uploading a world from Unity using \"Build & Publish Your World Online\", the \"Props that modify Player movement\" setting under \"Default Content Settings\" (which is configured via the web World Edit) gets reset to enabled every single time.\n\nIt is very tedious to reconfigure this in World Edit after every upload. Furthermore, if I forget to change it back, it directly affects the world's intended behavior and mechanics.\n\nCurrently, \"Default Content Settings\" cannot be managed within the VRCSDK Builder tab. I would highly appreciate it if you could implement either of the following solutions:\n\n1. Prevent this specific setting from being reset upon uploading from Unity.\n\n2. Allow us to edit \"Default Content Settings\" directly within the VRCSDK Builder tab so it syncs correctly.\n\nPlease consider this improvement. Thank you!\n\nEnvironment:\n\n- Unity 2022.3.22f1\n\n- VRCSDK 3.10.4",
